{
  "A six-month residency for artists who make Omarchy beautiful. Themes, plugins, and whatever else. The point is to let creativity flow with the support of the Omacom Foundation. Up to five seats at any one time.": "為讓 Omarchy 更美的藝術家提供六個月駐留計畫。主題、外掛，或任何其他作品。目標是在 Omacom Foundation 的支持下，讓創造力自由流淌。同期最多五個名額。",
  "The first residents": "首批駐留藝術家",
  "<a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Solitude and Last Horizon</a> both ship with Omarchy, and another twenty of his themes sit on <a href=\"/themes/\">the extras page</a> - more than anyone else has contributed: Batou, Oxo Carbon, Velvet Night, Rose of Dune, Shades of Jade, and on it goes. He&rsquo;s a mechanical engineer who became one of the defining aesthetic forces in this community, sits on <a href=\"/teams/\">Omarchy Core</a>, and helps steward <a href=\"https://plugins.omarchy.org/\">the plugin ecosystem</a>.": "<a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Solitude 和 Last Horizon</a> 都已內置於 Omarchy，<a href=\"/themes/\">額外主題頁面</a>還有他的二十款作品，比任何人貢獻的都多：Batou、Oxo Carbon、Velvet Night、Rose of Dune、Shades of Jade，等等。他從機械工程師成為社群審美的關鍵推動者，是 <a href=\"/teams/\">Omarchy Core</a> 成員，也參與維護<a href=\"https://plugins.omarchy.org/\">外掛生態</a>。",
  "Three of the themes that ship with Omarchy are his - <a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Lumon, Miasma, and Retro 82</a> - and another ten sit on <a href=\"/themes/\">the extras page</a>, from Batman to City-783 to Sakura Mochi. He works in whole palettes rather than one-off colour schemes, which is why his themes hold together across the terminal, Neovim, btop, and the shell instead of just looking good in a screenshot.": "三款內建主題出自他手：<a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Lumon、Miasma 和 Retro 82</a>。<a href=\"/themes/\">額外主題頁面</a>還有十款，從 Batman、City-783 到 Sakura Mochi。他設計完整的調色盤，而非一次性的配色，因此主題在終端、Neovim、btop 和 shell 中都協調一致，不只是截圖好看。",
  "He drew the Omarchy logo, which is reason enough, and he built <a href=\"https://github.com/tahayvr/omarchist\">Omarchist</a>, the GUI for making your own themes without touching a config file. <a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Matte Black</a> is his and ships with Omarchy, along with Gold Rush, Sunset Drive, and VHS 80 on <a href=\"/themes/\">the extras page</a>.": "他繪製了 Omarchy 標誌，僅這一點就足夠了；他還開發了 <a href=\"https://github.com/tahayvr/omarchist\">Omarchist</a>，讓你不碰設定檔就能製作主題的圖形工具。內建的 <a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Matte Black</a> 出自他手，<a href=\"/themes/\">額外主題頁面</a>還有 Gold Rush、Sunset Drive 和 VHS 80。",
  "Remaining seats by invitation": "其餘名額採用邀請制",
  "What it comes with": "我們提供什麼",
  "<span><strong>$2,500/month</strong> for the full six months.</span>": "<span>整個六個月，每月提供 <strong>2,500 美元</strong>。</span>",
  "<span><strong>Token account</strong> so the agents never need to stop.</span>": "<span><strong>Token 帳戶</strong>，讓 Agent 無需停工。</span>",
  "<span><strong>Permanent recognition</strong> as AIR alumni when six months are up.</span>": "<span>六個月結束後，作為 AIR 校友獲得<strong>永久認可</strong>。</span>",
  "The nonprofit funding the development, maintenance, and spread of Omarchy.<br>Interested in becoming a founding or distinguished patron? Write <a href=\"mailto:david@omarchy.org\">david@omarchy.org</a>.": "資助 Omarchy 開發、維護與傳播的非營利基金會。<br>有興趣成為創始或傑出贊助人？請聯絡 <a href=\"mailto:david@omarchy.org\">david@omarchy.org</a>。",
  "Patrons": "贊助人",
  "The foundation is funded by its patrons: twelve Founding Patrons contributing $1,000,000 each, Distinguished Patrons at $100,000, Distinguished Corporate Patrons at $100,000 a year - and soon a tier open to everyone.": "基金會由贊助人支持：十二位創始贊助人各捐助 1,000,000 美元，傑出贊助人各捐助 100,000 美元，傑出企業贊助人每年捐助 100,000 美元，很快還將開放人人可參與的等級。",
  "Sponsorships": "專案資助",
  "Multi-year sponsorships for the projects Omarchy is built on - Hyprland, Quickshell, and mise - so the people behind them can work without thinking about fundraising.": "為 Omarchy 所依賴的 Hyprland、Quickshell 和 mise 提供多年資助，讓開發者專注工作，不必為籌款操心。",
  "Artists in Residence": "駐留藝術家",
  "Omarchy AIR pays artists a six-month stipend to work freely on themes, plugins, and whatever else makes the system beautiful.": "Omarchy AIR 為藝術家提供六個月津貼，讓他們自由創作主題、外掛，以及任何能讓系統更美的作品。",
  "<a href=\"#founding-patrons\">Founding Patrons</a>": "<a href=\"#founding-patrons\">創始贊助人</a>",
  "Each contributing $1,000,000.": "每位捐助 1,000,000 美元。",
  "<a href=\"https://oligarchy.fyi\">Elite capital. Public code.</a>": "<a href=\"https://oligarchy.fyi\">精英的資本。大眾的程式碼。</a>",
  "<a href=\"#founding-token-patrons\">Founding Corporate Patrons</a>": "<a href=\"#founding-token-patrons\">創始企業贊助人</a>",
  "Each contributing $1,000,000/year for three years or $1,500,000 in tokens with option for refill.": "每家每年捐助 1,000,000 美元，持續三年；或提供可追加的 1,500,000 美元 token。",
  "<a href=\"#distinguished-patrons\">Distinguished Patrons</a>": "<a href=\"#distinguished-patrons\">傑出贊助人</a>",
  "Each contributing $100,000.": "每位捐助 100,000 美元。",
  "<a href=\"#distinguished-corporate-patrons\">Distinguished Corporate Patrons</a>": "<a href=\"#distinguished-corporate-patrons\">傑出企業贊助人</a>",
  "Each contributing $100,000/year for three years or $150,000 in tokens with option for refill.": "每家每年捐助 100,000 美元，持續三年；或提供可追加的 150,000 美元 token。",
  "<a href=\"#become-a-patron\">Become a Founding or Distinguished Patron</a>": "<a href=\"#become-a-patron\">成為創始或傑出贊助人</a>",
  "Interested in becoming a founding or distinguished patron? Write <a href=\"mailto:david@omarchy.org\">david@omarchy.org</a>.": "有興趣成為創始或傑出贊助人？請聯絡 <a href=\"mailto:david@omarchy.org\">david@omarchy.org</a>。",
  "<a href=\"#everyone\">All Patrons</a>": "<a href=\"#everyone\">全部贊助人</a>",
  "Each contributing as they see fit. Open for everyone.<br><a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">Become a patron</a> and <a href=\"/patrons/badges/\">collect your badge</a>.": "按自己的意願捐助，向所有人開放。<br><a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">成為贊助人</a>，<a href=\"/patrons/badges/\">領取徽章</a>。",
  "Every patron of the Omacom Foundation gets a digital rally credential to show for it. There's a badge for your website, a card for your socials, and wallpapers for your desktop and your phone. Four classes, one for each <a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">tier of patronage</a>. Pick your stage!": "每位 Omacom Foundation 贊助人都能獲得一份數位拉力賽憑證。包括網站徽章、社交卡片，以及桌面和手機桌布。四個組別，對應四檔<a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">贊助等級</a>。選好你的賽段！",
  "Forest Stage &middot; $16": "森林賽段 &middot; 16 美元",
  "The entry class. Green foil, gravel flying, and a Quattro heading into the trees. Sixteen bucks gets you on the team.": "入門組。綠色箔光、飛濺的砂石，一輛 Quattro 駛入林間。十六美元就能加入車隊。",
  "Mountain Hairpin &middot; $256": "山地髮夾彎 &middot; 256 美元",
  "Blue foil and a dusty hairpin high up the mountain. This is the class for those who want to put some real weight behind the mission.": "藍色箔光，高山髮夾彎上揚起的塵土。為願意給這項使命提供有力支持的人準備。",
  "Service Park &middot; $2,048": "維修區 &middot; 2,048 美元",
  "Violet foil under the floodlights of the service park, where the car gets rebuilt between stages. Two thousand dollars keeps a lot of open-source developers in the race.": "維修區燈光下的紫色箔光，賽車在賽段之間重新整備。兩千美元能讓許多開源開發者繼續參賽。",
  "Night Stage &middot; $8,192": "夜間賽段 &middot; 8,192 美元",
  "Magenta foil, four headlights, and a night stage carved out of the mountainside. The top class of open patronage. Thank you!": "洋紅色箔光、四盞頭燈，以及沿山坡開闢的夜間賽道。公開贊助中的最高組別。謝謝你！",
  "<a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">Become a patron</a> to claim yours. Artwork by <a href=\"https://github.com/OldJobobo\">OldJobobo</a>, <a href=\"/air/\">Artist in Residence</a>.": "<a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">成為贊助人</a>即可領取。作品來自<a href=\"/air/\">駐留藝術家</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/OldJobobo\">OldJobobo</a>。",
  "Report a vulnerability": "報告漏洞",
  "If you believe you&rsquo;ve found a security vulnerability in Omarchy, please tell the <a href=\"/teams/#security\">Omarchy Security Team</a> privately so we have an opportunity to investigate and fix it before it is made public.": "如果你認為發現了 Omarchy 安全漏洞，請私下告知 <a href=\"/teams/#security\">Omarchy Security 團隊</a>，讓我們有機會在公開前調查並修復。",
  "Please don&rsquo;t report potential vulnerabilities publicly in GitHub Issues, Discord, or social media before they&rsquo;ve been resolved.": "請不要在問題解決前，將潛在漏洞公開發布到 GitHub Issues、Discord 或社交媒體。",
  "What is a vulnerability?": "什麼是漏洞？",
  "We consider a bug a security vulnerability when it can be exploited to cross a meaningful security boundary: an untrusted or lower-privileged party gains access, permissions, or control they didn&rsquo;t already have.": "當一個錯誤可被利用來跨越實質性的安全邊界時，我們將其視為安全漏洞：不受信任或許可權較低的一方，獲得原本不具備的訪問權、許可權或控制能力。",
  "Code that could be more robust but does not cross a security boundary is an improvement rather than a security vulnerability. We may still merge a proposed fix and credit the reporter in our release notes.": "可以更健壯、但不跨越安全邊界的程式碼屬於改進事項，而非安全漏洞。我們仍可能合入修復，並在發行說明中感謝報告者。",
  "Eligibility for our <a href=\"/security/credits/\">security credits</a> page depends on whether a report identifies a confirmed security vulnerability, not on its severity.": "能否列入<a href=\"/security/credits/\">安全貢獻者</a>頁面，取決於報告是否指出了經確認的安全漏洞，而不是漏洞的嚴重程度。",
  "What to include": "報告應包含什麼",
  "Give us enough information to understand and reproduce the issue:": "請提供足夠的資訊，讓我們理解並復現問題：",
  "The affected component and Omarchy version.": "受影響的元件與 Omarchy 版本。",
  "An explanation of what an attacker can do before and after exploitation.": "說明攻擊者在利用漏洞前後分別能做什麼。",
  "Steps to reproduce the issue and any proof of concept.": "復現步驟，以及任何概念驗證程式碼。",
  "Your preferred contact details for follow-up.": "你希望用於後續溝通的聯絡方式。",
  "Responsible disclosure": "負責任的披露",
  "Please act in good faith while investigating and reporting vulnerabilities:": "調查和報告漏洞時，請秉持善意：",
  "Only test systems and accounts you own or have explicit permission to test.": "僅測試你擁有或獲得明確授權的系統與帳戶。",
  "Avoid privacy violations, disruption, data destruction, and service degradation.": "避免侵犯隱私、造成中斷、破壞資料或降低服務品質。",
  "Don&rsquo;t exploit a vulnerability beyond what is needed to demonstrate it.": "不要超出證明漏洞所必需的範圍進行利用。",
  "Give us a reasonable opportunity to investigate and address the issue before publishing details.": "公開詳情前，請給我們合理的調查與處理機會。",
  "We&rsquo;ll review your report and keep you informed as we&rsquo;re able while we work toward a resolution.": "我們會審閱報告，並在解決問題期間儘可能向你更新進展。",
  "Credits": "致謝",
  "Researchers who privately report a confirmed security vulnerability and give us the chance to ship a fix are thanked on the <a href=\"/security/credits/\">security credits</a> page. Accepted improvements that don&rsquo;t cross a security boundary may still be credited in our release notes.": "私下報告已確認的安全漏洞，並讓我們有機會發布修復的研究者，將獲列入<a href=\"/security/credits/\">安全貢獻者</a>頁面。未跨越安全邊界但被採納的改進，也可能在發行說明中獲得致謝。",
  "Credits link to each reporter&rsquo;s X profile and show their avatar. For duplicate reports, only the first reporter is eligible for credit.": "致謝會展示報告者頭像並連結其 X 主頁。對於重複報告，僅首位報告者可獲列名。",
  "Regular bugs and support": "普通錯誤與求助",
  "For anything that isn&rsquo;t a security vulnerability, please use the <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/issues\">Omarchy issue tracker</a>.": "對於非安全漏洞的問題，請使用 <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/issues\">Omarchy 問題跟蹤器</a>。",
  "They found it, told us privately, and waited for the patch": "他們發現問題，私下告知，並等待補丁",
  "Found something? <a href=\"/security/\">Report it privately</a>. The first reporter of a confirmed vulnerability is credited here.": "發現了什麼？請<a href=\"/security/\">私下報告</a>。首位報告已確認漏洞的人會在這裡獲得致謝。",
  "Exclusive": "獨家",
  "The tiling Wayland compositor that has been at the heart of Omarchy since day one, and one of its three core technologies. The sponsorship lets Vaxry work on it without having to think about commercial development or fundraising - and it freed the existing Hyprperks program to be released for everyone, for free. The deal runs three years, with an option for another two, and starts October 10.": "這款平鋪式 Wayland 合成器從第一天起就是 Omarchy 的核心，也是三大基礎技術之一。贊助讓 Vaxry 無需考慮商業開發或籌款，專心投入，也讓現有 Hyprperks 得以免費向所有人開放。協議從 10 月 10 日開始，為期三年，可再延長兩年。",
  "Premier": "主要",
  "The desktop construction kit the Omarchy shell is built on: one long-running process drawing the bar, the menu, the notifications, the OSDs and the lock screen. It shipped in Quattro, and over a thousand plugins followed in the first week. Termed for three years out the gate.": "Omarchy shell 的桌面構建工具包：一個常駐程序繪製狀態列、選單、通知、OSD 和鎖屏。它隨 Quattro 推出，第一週就出現了超過一千款外掛。協議一開始便籤訂三年。",
  "The tool that manages the language runtimes and, just as importantly, ships every coding-agent CLI as a lazy-loading stub. A new harness is one command away instead of a packaging project - which is what keeps Omarchy moving at the pace agent tooling actually ships.": "這款工具管理語言執行時，更同樣重要的是，將每個程式設計 Agent CLI 作為按需載入的啟動器提供。新 Agent 環境只需一條命令，不用另做打包專案，讓 Omarchy 跟得上 Agent 工具的實際發布速度。",
  "A 2011 ThinkPad X220. Just 2GB of RAM. Watch Omarchy run with room to spare.": "2011 年的 ThinkPad X220，僅有 2GB 記憶體。看看 Omarchy 如何遊刃有餘地執行。",
  "David Heinemeier Hansson takes Omarchy for a spin on a very modest machine.": "David Heinemeier Hansson 在一臺規格十分樸素的電腦上試用 Omarchy。",
  "You don't need a new computer to try Omarchy. Give the one you already have a second life.": "試用 Omarchy 不需要新電腦。讓手頭的老機器煥發新生。",
  "Coming 2026": "將於 2026 年推出",
  "Early Aesthetics": "早期美學",
  "There's only so much you can do with GNOME, but I did what I could.": "GNOME 能做的有限，但我盡力了。",
  "Neovim and Zellij out of the box.": "開箱即用的 Neovim 和 Zellij。",
  "Even then, one command could re-theme multiple apps.": "即使在當時，一條命令也能為多個應用更換主題。",
  "The road to Omarchy": "通往 Omarchy 的路",
  "Omakub proved the thesis: give developers a beautiful, complete Linux out of the box, and they&rsquo;ll show up! Tens of thousands did.": "Omakub 證明了這個想法：給開發者一個開箱即用、美觀完整的 Linux，他們就會來！數萬人來了。",
  "But it also found the ceiling. Omakub was a layer of opinion on top of Ubuntu and GNOME, and those come with strong opinions of their own. The ideas I actually cared about - tiling, everything on the keyboard, a system that treats the terminal as the center of the universe - kept fighting the platform instead of flowing from it.": "但它也碰到了天花板。Omakub 在 Ubuntu 和 GNOME 之上疊加自己的主張，而它們本身也有很強的主張。我真正關心的東西——平鋪視窗、全鍵盤操作、以終端為宇宙中心的系統——總是在與平台對抗，而不是從平台自然生長。",
  "So the omakase moved from Ubuntu to Arch, from GNOME to Hyprland, and became <a href=\"/\">Omarchy</a>. Not a layer on top of somebody else&rsquo;s distribution, but the whole meal. Everything Omakub was reaching for, without asking anyone&rsquo;s permission first.": "於是，omakase 從 Ubuntu 轉向 Arch，從 GNOME 轉向 Hyprland，成為 <a href=\"/\">Omarchy</a>。不再只是別人發行版上的一層，而是整桌菜。Omakub 想實現的一切，無需先徵求任何人的許可。",
  "The retirement home is staffed": "退休之後，也有人照看",
  "Omakub itself is now retired. The repositories are archived on GitHub - <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omakub\">omakub</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omakub-site\">omakub-site</a>. But good ideas don&rsquo;t retire, they get forked! <a href=\"https://omabuntu.omakasui.org/\">Omabuntu</a> is a community fork continuing on the omakase-Ubuntu thread. If Arch is a step too far and Ubuntu is home, that&rsquo;s where you should go.": "Omakub 現已退休。GitHub 倉庫 <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omakub\">omakub</a> 和 <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omakub-site\">omakub-site</a> 已歸檔。但好想法不會退休，只會被分叉！<a href=\"https://omabuntu.omakasui.org/\">Omabuntu</a> 是延續 omakase-Ubuntu 路線的社群分支。如果 Arch 跨度太大，而 Ubuntu 才是熟悉的家，那就去那裡。",
  "Thanks to everyone who ran it, contributed to it, and showed off their desktops. Omakub walked so Omarchy could run.": "感謝所有使用它、貢獻它、展示自己桌面的人。Omakub 學會了走，Omarchy 才能奔跑。",
  "Wordmark": "文字標識",
  "OMA Logo": "OMA 標誌",
  "Trademark": "商標",
  "Omarchy is a pending trademark. All rights reserved.": "Omarchy 商標正在申請中。保留所有權利。",
  "Write <a href=\"mailto:foundation@omarchy.org\">foundation@omarchy.org</a> for partnerships.": "合作請聯絡 <a href=\"mailto:foundation@omarchy.org\">foundation@omarchy.org</a>。",
